 using the  widespread support for the protests  among the middle classes as an excuse to  go on the rampage  it does not take long for the state to  respond  gabby is giving an interview at the  independent radio station radio caracas  she has an hour to promote the students  cause  has all means of repression and has  seized all the wealth of the country for  itself  listeners can take part in the  discussion most want to put questions  directly to the opposition they don't  trust the state media  our friend was standing by a barricade  when the cowards from the national guard  came and attacked and beat him but  luckily he could be freed  most callers sympathize with the  students  this one says that she prays daily for  their safety and protection and urges  them to keep on doing what they're doing  the venezuelans and the students don't  believe in a peace like in cuba  there they live in peace but without  freedom and without freedom and justice  says gabi then peace is just an illusion  the church agrees  peace can only follow from truth from  justice and freedom one after the other  that's why we're fighting on the streets  with three olympic games under her belt  alejandra is now preparing for rio 2016  fencing is her sporting passion but her  political heart belongs to hugo chavez  alejandra says he was like a father to  her and that she was like a daughter to  him  when her sporting career is over she  plans to work as a dentist she has  already successfully completed her  studies  and she has a fully equipped dental  practice purchased with the money she  earned as an olympic athlete  it doesn't cross her mind that the  opposition could succeed in overthrowing  the government she believes that the  poor will remain devoted to the  political ideology of chavez and she is  convinced that chavistas will still be  in power five years from now  in the past people didn't want to admit  that they were venezuelan she says today  they're proud and they're willing to  wear the national colors  they have learned how to fight for their  interests for their country for their  ideals  in five years we will be a very  enlightened people who have lived up to  our ideals  part of the population voted for the  chavista says they believed in them but  they were fooled and now they support us  we want to ensure that those in power  pay  dialogue could offer a way out of the  deadlock but neither side has been  serious about it so far  a dialogue with maduro who shoots at us  no chance


